          ":question/id": "62a798f9-3a3f-593e-8d90-d4fb1b723f5e",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-10645",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2z &=3 \\\\ -2x+y-3z &=-4 \\\\ 4x-3y+6z &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 & -4 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 6 & -8\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 & -4 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 6 & -8\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 6 & -8\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -20\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -14\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -14\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 31 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -14\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=31 \\\\ y &=16 \\\\ z &=-14.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSo, we have the solution $x=31$, $y=16$ and $z=-14.$ Or, in vector form $\u27e831,16,-14\u27e9.$"
