          ":question/id": "cc172ce1-8b2c-5d68-83ff-3cd2b2af4b0f",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-10646",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y+z &=8 \\\\ 2x-3y+2z &=14 \\\\ 3x-6y+2z &=21\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 2 & 14 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 2 & 21\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 2 & 14 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 2 & 21\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 2 & 21\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :=(-1){R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=1 \\\\ y &=-2 \\\\ z &=3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSo, we have the solution $x=1$, $y=-2$ and $z=3.$ Or, in vector form $\u27e81,-2,3\u27e9.$"
        }
